# Coding Rules (STRICT)
You MUST follow these coding standards.
## General
- Use TypeScript for ALL code
- Use ESM (import/export)
- NEVER use require()
## File Design
- Keep files small and focused
- Separate responsibilities:
  - repository (DB access)
  - handler (IPC)
  - UI (React)
## Error Handling
- ALL IPC handlers MUST use try/catch
- ALWAYS return structured response:
Example:
{
  success: true,
  data: ...
}
or
{
  success: false,
  error: "message"
}
## Async Rules
- ALWAYS use async/await
- NEVER use .then()
## Naming
- variables → camelCase
- functions → camelCase
- components → PascalCase
- constants → UPPER_CASE
## React Rules
- Use functional components ONLY
- Use hooks
- NO class components
## State Management
- Prefer local state first
- Avoid global state unless necessary
## Code Quality
- NO console.log in production code
- Remove unused imports
- Avoid duplicate logic (reuse functions)
## Imports
- Use absolute imports if possible
- Keep import order clean:
  1. external libs
  2. shared
  3. local files
## Enforcement
If code violates these rules:
- You MUST refactor it to follow the rules
